# The working tree matches what ships.
#
# core.autocrlf=true was checking text files out as CRLF while git stored — and
# Cloudflare serves — LF. That is invisible until something fingerprints the
# files: sw.js's SHELL_DIGEST hashed the working tree, so the digest recorded
# from one worktree described bytes that never reached a player, and every file
# looked changed when the next person landed from a worktree checked out the
# other way. Both are avoided by not having two answers in the first place.
#
# Blobs are already LF, so this normalises the checkout rather than the history.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries never get line-ending treatment, said explicitly rather than left to
# content sniffing — a mangled woff2 or png is a bug nobody looks for.
*.png    binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ogg    binary
*.webm   binary
